WEBVTT

00:00:09.949 --> 00:00:13.913
Take your brother outside as
fast as you can! Now Dean! Go!

00:00:15.755 --> 00:00:17.558
Mary! No!

00:00:20.082 --> 00:00:21.864
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:24.802
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:24.915 --> 00:00:26.237
Jess excuse us.

00:00:28.798 --> 00:00:30.191
I swore I was done hunting,

00:00:30.824 --> 00:00:31.541
For good.

00:00:31.613 --> 00:00:32.484
I can't do this alone.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:35.665
Now you're taking off the middle of the
night to spend the week-End with them.

00:00:35.666 --> 00:00:38.166
Hey, everything's gonna be OK.

00:00:38.209 --> 00:00:39.479
I promise.

00:00:41.354 --> 00:00:42.768
You think mom would
have wanted this for us?

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:44.716
Dean, we were raised like warriors.

00:00:44.771 --> 00:00:47.855
You have a responsability.
To dad and his cruisade.

00:00:47.988 --> 00:00:51.400
Even if you do find the thing
that killed her, mom's gone

00:00:51.796 --> 00:00:53.966
And she isn't coming back.

00:00:54.503 --> 00:00:56.632
Don't talk about her like that.

00:00:57.778 --> 00:00:58.735
Dad's gone.

00:00:58.796 --> 00:01:00.439
I've got his journal.
He left me a message.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.754
It's coordinates he
left us. It's weird, man.

00:01:02.837 --> 00:01:03.431
Hey, Dean,

00:01:03.541 --> 00:01:04.495
What I said earlier,

00:01:04.573 --> 00:01:05.919
I'm sorry.

00:01:06.498 --> 00:01:07.922
No chick-Flick moments.

00:01:09.694 --> 00:01:10.727
Yes.

00:01:20.085 --> 00:01:21.149
No!

00:01:32.228 --> 00:01:34.762
We got work to do.

00:02:13.209 --> 00:02:14.629
Dude, you're cheating.

00:02:14.956 --> 00:02:17.126
No, you just suck.

00:02:23.391 --> 00:02:26.433
Hey, Hailey. Day six. We're
still out near Black Water Ridge.

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:30.434
We're fine, keeping safe, so
don't worry. Talk to you tomorrow.

00:02:39.761 --> 00:02:42.150
Hey, where you going?
My moment of victory.

00:02:42.272 --> 00:02:43.815
Nature calls.

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.022
Brad?

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:30.316
Gary, what's going on?

00:04:48.235 --> 00:04:50.896
I am, um...

00:04:51.598 --> 00:04:57.030
You always said roses were
lame, so, I brought you, uh...

00:05:11.897 --> 00:05:13.316
Jess...

00:05:14.376 --> 00:05:15.658
Oh, god.

00:05:20.359 --> 00:05:22.024
I should have protected you.

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:25.072
I should have told you the truth.

00:05:41.724 --> 00:05:43.103
You okay?

00:05:43.512 --> 00:05:44.836
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:05:45.723 --> 00:05:47.115
Another nightmare?

00:05:52.983 --> 00:05:54.744
Want to drive for a while?

00:05:57.246 --> 00:06:00.440
In your whole life, you
never once asked me that.

00:06:00.898 --> 00:06:03.333
Just thought you might
want to. Never mind.

00:06:04.059 --> 00:06:05.154
Look, man,

00:06:05.707 --> 00:06:08.038
You're worried about
me. I get it, and ...

00:06:08.226 --> 00:06:11.934
Thank you, but I'm perfectly okay.

00:06:15.006 --> 00:06:17.415
All right. Where are we?

00:06:17.822 --> 00:06:20.497
We are just outside of Grand Junction.

00:06:24.666 --> 00:06:28.014
You know what? Maybe we shouldn't
have left Stanford so soon.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:32.082
Sam, we dug around there for a
week. We came up with nothing.

00:06:32.446 --> 00:06:36.201
If you want to find the thing that
killed Jessica... Got to find dad first.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:41.255
Dad disappearing, and this thing
showing up again after 20 years?

00:06:41.494 --> 00:06:43.340
It's no coincidence.

00:06:43.778 --> 00:06:47.157
Dad will have answers. He'll
know what to do. It's weird, man.

00:06:47.517 --> 00:06:50.943
These coordinates he left
us, this Black Water Ridge...

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:53.550
What about it? There's nothing there.

00:06:54.144 --> 00:06:56.621
It's just woods.

00:06:58.357 --> 00:07:01.158
Why is he sending us to
the middle of nowhere?

00:07:08.105 --> 00:07:10.405
So Black Water Ridge is pretty remote.

00:07:10.514 --> 00:07:13.881
It's cut off by these canyons
here --Rough terrain, dense forest,

00:07:13.882 --> 00:07:16.382
Abandoned silver and gold
mines all over the place...

00:07:16.507 --> 00:07:19.797
Dude, check out the size
of this friggin' bear.

00:07:22.332 --> 00:07:25.977
And a dozen or more
grizzlies in the area.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:28.767
It's no nature hike, that's for sure.

00:07:29.158 --> 00:07:32.897
You boys aren't planning to go out
near Black Water Ridge, by any chance?

00:07:33.163 --> 00:07:38.284
Oh, no, sir. We're environmental-Study majors
from U.C. Boulder-Just working on a paper.

00:07:38.378 --> 00:07:39.926
Recycle, man.

00:07:40.229 --> 00:07:41.371
Bull.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.954
You're friends with
that Hailey girl, right?

00:07:46.273 --> 00:07:46.899
Yes.

00:07:47.337 --> 00:07:48.901
Yes, we are.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:51.452
Ranger... Wilkinson.

00:07:52.285 --> 00:07:54.505
Well, I will tell you
exactly what I told her.

00:07:54.506 --> 00:07:59.906
Her brother filled out a backcountry permit saying
he wouldn't be back from Black Water until the 24th.

00:08:00.008 --> 00:08:02.558
So it's not exactly a
missing persons now, is it?

00:08:03.168 --> 00:08:06.250
Tell that girl to quit worrying.
I'm sure her brother's just fine.

00:08:06.407 --> 00:08:07.737
We will.

00:08:08.519 --> 00:08:10.569
Well, that Hailey girl's
quite a pistol, huh?

00:08:10.698 --> 00:08:12.404
That is putting it mildly.

00:08:12.565 --> 00:08:16.969
Actually, you know what would help is if I
could show her a copy of that backcountry permit.

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:20.670
You know, so she could see
her brother's return date.

00:08:21.973 --> 00:08:24.445
Yeah. Heh heh.

00:08:24.586 --> 00:08:26.385
What, are you cruising
for a hookup or something?

00:08:26.447 --> 00:08:27.198
What do you mean?

00:08:27.312 --> 00:08:29.851
The coordinates point to Black Water
Ridge. So what are we waiting for?

00:08:29.852 --> 00:08:33.352
Let's just go find dad.
Why even talk to this girl?

00:08:33.461 --> 00:08:37.669
I don't know, maybe we should know what we're
walking into before we actually walk into it.

00:08:38.591 --> 00:08:39.530
What?

00:08:39.608 --> 00:08:42.910
Since when are you all "shoot
first, ask questions later" anyway?

00:08:43.176 --> 00:08:44.599
Since now.

00:08:46.524 --> 00:08:48.057
Oh, really?

00:08:51.563 --> 00:08:53.159
You must be Hailey Collins.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:57.302
I'm Dean, this is Sam. We're rangers with the
park service. Ranger Wilkinson sent us over.

00:08:57.303 --> 00:09:01.003
We wanted to ask you some
questions about your brother Tommy.

00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:03.756
Let me see some I.D.

00:09:06.659 --> 00:09:07.911
There you go.

00:09:14.701 --> 00:09:17.439
Come on in. Thanks.

00:09:18.644 --> 00:09:19.504
That yours?

00:09:19.739 --> 00:09:20.318
Yeah.

00:09:20.459 --> 00:09:21.570
Nice car.

00:09:26.491 --> 00:09:30.324
So, if Tommy's not due back for a
while, how do you know something's wrong?

00:09:30.563 --> 00:09:34.791
He checks in every day by cell. He
e-Mails photos, stupid little videos.

00:09:34.792 --> 00:09:37.292
But we haven't heard anything
in over three days now.

00:09:37.553 --> 00:09:39.493
Well, maybe he can't get cell reception.

00:09:39.795 --> 00:09:41.485
He's got a satellite phone, too.

00:09:41.876 --> 00:09:46.538
Could it be he's just having fun and
forgot to check in? He wouldn't do that.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.944
Our parents are gone. It's
just my two brothers and me.

00:09:50.945 --> 00:09:53.445
We all keep pretty
close tabs on each other.

00:09:54.023 --> 00:09:56.870
Can I see the pictures
he sent you? Yeah.

00:09:57.762 --> 00:09:59.186
That's Tommy.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:08.544
Hey, Hailey. Day six. We're
still out near Black Water Ridge.

00:10:08.545 --> 00:10:12.545
We're fine, keeping safe, so don't
worry, okay? Talk to you tomorrow.

00:10:14.222 --> 00:10:17.464
We'll find your brother. We're heading
out to Black Water Ridge first thing.

00:10:17.465 --> 00:10:19.965
Then maybe I'll see you there.

00:10:20.918 --> 00:10:21.779
Look.

00:10:21.971 --> 00:10:23.817
I can't sit around here anymore,

00:10:24.052 --> 00:10:27.916
So I hired a guide. I'm heading out in the
morning, and I'm gonna find Tommy myself.

00:10:28.672 --> 00:10:30.951
I think I know how you feel.

00:10:33.084 --> 00:10:35.400
Hey, you mind forwarding these to me?

00:10:35.666 --> 00:10:36.636
Sure.

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:44.909
So, Black Water Ridge doesn't get a
lot of traffic-Local campers mostly--

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:49.910
But, still, this past april, two hikers went
missing out there. They were never found.

00:10:49.977 --> 00:10:51.291
Any before that?

00:10:51.369 --> 00:10:51.980
Yeah.

00:10:52.027 --> 00:10:55.067
In 1982, eight different people
all vanished in the same year.

00:10:55.068 --> 00:10:57.268
Authorities said it
was a grizzly attack.

00:10:57.268 --> 00:11:02.468
And, again, in 1959, and
again, before that, in 1936.

00:11:02.577 --> 00:11:05.844
Every 23 years, just like clockwork.

00:11:06.285 --> 00:11:07.804
Okay, watch this.

00:11:08.033 --> 00:11:09.650
Here's the clincher.

00:11:10.538 --> 00:11:15.438
I downloaded that guy Tommy's
video to the laptop. Check this out.

00:11:16.778 --> 00:11:18.264
Do it again.

00:11:21.358 --> 00:11:26.699
That's three frames. It's a fraction of a
second. Whatever that thing is, it can move.

00:11:27.663 --> 00:11:29.999
I told you something weird was going on.

00:11:30.326 --> 00:11:32.972
Yeah. I got one more thing.

00:11:33.098 --> 00:11:38.030
In '59, one camper survived the
supposed grizzly attack, just a kid

00:11:38.227 --> 00:11:40.317
Barely crawled out of the woods alive.

00:11:40.657 --> 00:11:42.065
Is there a name?

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:46.684
Look, ranger, I don't know why
you're asking me about this.

00:11:46.826 --> 00:11:49.673
It's public record. I was a kid.

00:11:49.876 --> 00:11:52.223
My parents got mauled by a... grizzly?

00:11:52.418 --> 00:11:53.904
That's what attacked them?

00:12:02.215 --> 00:12:04.452
The other people that
went missing that year,

00:12:04.656 --> 00:12:06.690
Those bear attacks, too?

00:12:08.928 --> 00:12:11.432
What about all the people
that went missing this year?

00:12:12.151 --> 00:12:13.747
Same thing?

00:12:15.848 --> 00:12:19.990
If we knew what we were dealing
with, we might be able to stop it.

00:12:21.919 --> 00:12:24.547
I seriously doubt that.

00:12:24.954 --> 00:12:26.033
Anyways,

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:29.689
I don't see the
difference it would make.

00:12:30.972 --> 00:12:32.849
You wouldn't believe me.

00:12:33.178 --> 00:12:35.399
Nobody ever did.

00:12:38.135 --> 00:12:39.622
Mr. Shaw

00:12:42.688 --> 00:12:44.565
What did you see?

00:12:49.146 --> 00:12:50.585
Nothing.

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:55.404
It moved too fast to see.

00:12:55.451 --> 00:12:57.062
It hid too well.

00:12:57.176 --> 00:12:58.663
I heard it, though.

00:12:59.257 --> 00:13:01.228
A roar

00:13:02.981 --> 00:13:03.873
Like ...

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:07.526
No man or animal I ever heard.

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:09.619
It came at night?

00:13:10.308 --> 00:13:12.185
Got inside your tent?

00:13:12.503 --> 00:13:14.991
It got inside our cabin.

00:13:15.789 --> 00:13:19.669
I was sleeping in front of
the fireplace when it came in.

00:13:20.315 --> 00:13:23.397
It didn't smash a
window or break the door,

00:13:24.043 --> 00:13:26.062
It unlocked it.

00:13:26.844 --> 00:13:30.693
Do you know of a bear that
could do something like that?

00:13:31.355 --> 00:13:35.188
I didn't even wake up until
I heard my parents screaming.

00:13:35.423 --> 00:13:36.565
It killed them?

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:38.974
Dragged them off into the night.

00:13:41.508 --> 00:13:46.843
Why it left me alive --I've been
asking myself that ever since.

00:13:51.275 --> 00:13:53.450
It did leave me this, though.

00:14:03.407 --> 00:14:07.271
There's something evil in those woods.

00:14:10.009 --> 00:14:12.403
It was some sort of a demon.

00:14:12.877 --> 00:14:16.401
Spirits and demons don't have to unlock
doors. They just go through the walls.

00:14:16.402 --> 00:14:19.402
So it's probably something
else -Something corporeal.

00:14:19.531 --> 00:14:20.626
"Corporeal"?

00:14:20.892 --> 00:14:22.144
Excuse me, professor.

00:14:22.289 --> 00:14:24.151
Shut up. So, what do you think?

00:14:24.667 --> 00:14:27.108
The claws, the speed that it moves.

00:14:27.436 --> 00:14:29.580
It could be a skinwalker,
maybe a black dog

00:14:29.734 --> 00:14:34.365
Whatever we're talking about, we're talking
about a creature, and it's corporeal,

00:14:34.506 --> 00:14:36.623
Which means we can kill it.

00:14:53.770 --> 00:14:56.023
We cannot let that
Hailey girl go out there.

00:14:56.085 --> 00:14:59.843
Oh yeah, what are we gonna tell her she can't go
into the woods because of a big, scary monster?

00:14:59.844 --> 00:15:01.844
Yeah.

00:15:02.583 --> 00:15:03.929
Her brother's missing, Sam.

00:15:04.132 --> 00:15:05.837
She's not just gonna sit this out.

00:15:06.135 --> 00:15:10.333
No, we go with her, we protect her, and we keep
our eyes peeled for our fuzzy predator friend

00:15:10.427 --> 00:15:12.351
So finding dad's not enough?

00:15:14.749 --> 00:15:16.955
Now we got to babysit, too?

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:20.726
What?

00:15:22.024 --> 00:15:23.057
Nothing.

00:15:30.091 --> 00:15:33.193
I'll tell you again. I
don't think ben should come.

00:15:33.804 --> 00:15:35.008
Roy...

00:15:35.483 --> 00:15:40.239
Look, you're paying me good money to keep
everybody safe. I think Ben's safest at home.

00:15:50.503 --> 00:15:52.145
You guys got room for two more?

00:15:52.338 --> 00:15:54.012
You want to come with us?

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:54.998
Who are these guys?

00:15:55.045 --> 00:15:58.409
Apparently, this is all the
park service could muster up.

00:15:58.460 --> 00:15:59.775
You're rangers?

00:15:59.822 --> 00:16:00.666
That's right.

00:16:00.823 --> 00:16:03.874
And you're hiking out
in biker boots and jeans?

00:16:05.141 --> 00:16:07.801
Well, sweet heart, I don't do shorts.

00:16:09.767 --> 00:16:14.163
Oh, you think this is funny? It's dangerous
backcountry out there. Her brother might be hurt.

00:16:16.541 --> 00:16:19.091
Believe me, I know how
dangerous it can be.

00:16:19.652 --> 00:16:22.124
We just want to help them
find their brother. That's all.

00:17:20.554 --> 00:17:22.885
Roy, you said you did a little hunting.

00:17:23.156 --> 00:17:25.143
Yeah, more than a little.

00:17:27.052 --> 00:17:28.761
What kind of furry critters do you hunt?

00:17:28.918 --> 00:17:31.405
Mostly buck. Sometimes bear.

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:36.443
Tell me, uh, Bambi or
Yogi ever hunt you back?

00:17:40.456 --> 00:17:42.678
What you doing, Roy?

00:17:48.674 --> 00:17:51.303
You should watch where
you're stepping... ranger.

00:17:55.199 --> 00:17:57.311
It's a bear trap.

00:18:03.423 --> 00:18:05.707
You didn't pack any provisions.

00:18:05.816 --> 00:18:07.646
You guys are carrying a duffel bag.

00:18:07.756 --> 00:18:10.822
You're not rangers, so
who the hell are you?

00:18:19.392 --> 00:18:21.316
Sam and I are brothers,

00:18:21.614 --> 00:18:23.241
And we're looking for our father.

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:24.876
He might be here. We don't know.

00:18:25.016 --> 00:18:27.989
I just figured that you and
me, we're in the same boat.

00:18:29.637 --> 00:18:33.282
Why didn't you just tell me that
from the start? I'm telling you now.

00:18:33.767 --> 00:18:36.850
Besides, it's probably the most
honest I've ever been with a woman...

00:18:37.397 --> 00:18:38.664
Ever.

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:41.391
So, we okay?

00:18:45.381 --> 00:18:47.196
Yeah, okay.

00:18:47.717 --> 00:18:50.048
And what do you mean I
didn't pack provisions?

00:19:06.827 --> 00:19:08.282
This is it.

00:19:08.689 --> 00:19:09.893
Black Water Ridge.

00:19:09.956 --> 00:19:11.818
What coordinates are we at?

00:19:15.776 --> 00:19:17.987
35 and minus 111.

00:19:23.322 --> 00:19:24.323
You hear that?

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:25.543
Yeah.

00:19:27.149 --> 00:19:28.901
Not even crickets.

00:19:29.668 --> 00:19:31.561
I'm gonna go take a look around.

00:19:31.926 --> 00:19:34.194
You shouldn't go off by yourself.

00:19:34.304 --> 00:19:37.746
That's sweet. Don't worry about me.

00:19:45.836 --> 00:19:49.701
All right, everybody
stays together. Let's go.

00:19:58.379 --> 00:20:00.413
Hailey! Over here!

00:20:08.007 --> 00:20:09.337
Oh, my god.

00:20:09.728 --> 00:20:11.496
Looks like a grizzly.

00:20:28.107 --> 00:20:29.280
Tommy?

00:20:31.079 --> 00:20:32.174
Tommy!

00:20:32.644 --> 00:20:35.151
Tommy! Shh... Shh...

00:20:35.945 --> 00:20:36.899
Why?

00:20:37.337 --> 00:20:38.964
Something might still be out there.

00:20:39.845 --> 00:20:40.878
Sam.

00:20:48.439 --> 00:20:50.931
The bodies were dragged
from the campsite.

00:20:52.042 --> 00:20:55.140
But here, the tracks just vanish.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:57.158
It's weird.

00:20:59.317 --> 00:21:01.570
I tell you what.

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:04.590
It's no skinwalker or black dog.

00:21:27.603 --> 00:21:29.981
Hey, he could still be alive.

00:21:33.876 --> 00:21:36.020
Help!

00:21:57.497 --> 00:22:00.329
It seemed like it was coming
from around here, didn't it?

00:22:06.306 --> 00:22:08.496
Everybody back to camp.

00:22:14.511 --> 00:22:16.075
Our packs!

00:22:16.717 --> 00:22:19.752
So much for my GPS
and my satellite phone.

00:22:19.866 --> 00:22:21.227
What the hell's going on?

00:22:21.321 --> 00:22:22.432
It's smart.

00:22:22.510 --> 00:22:24.950
It wants to cut us off
so we can't call for help.

00:22:25.169 --> 00:22:29.284
You mean someone --Some nut job
out there just stole all our gear.

00:22:29.367 --> 00:22:32.730
I need to speak with you... in private.

00:22:41.600 --> 00:22:44.151
Okay, let me see dad's journal.

00:22:49.978 --> 00:22:50.854
All right.

00:22:51.730 --> 00:22:52.794
Check that out.

00:22:53.921 --> 00:22:55.188
Oh, come on.

00:22:55.459 --> 00:22:59.363
Windigos are in the Minnesota woods or Northern
Michigan. I've never even heard of one this far west.

00:22:59.264 --> 00:23:05.364
Think about it, Dean -The claws,
the way it can mimic a human voice.

00:23:05.724 --> 00:23:06.710
Great.

00:23:07.367 --> 00:23:09.370
Well, then this is useless.

00:23:14.063 --> 00:23:16.269
We got to get these people to safety.

00:23:18.345 --> 00:23:21.130
All right, listen up. It's time to go.

00:23:21.412 --> 00:23:24.963
Things have gotten more complicated.

00:23:25.594 --> 00:23:25.985
What?

00:23:26.079 --> 00:23:28.598
Whatever's out there,
I think I can handle it.

00:23:28.660 --> 00:23:33.213
If you shoot this thing, you're just
gonna make it mad. We have to leave now.

00:23:33.244 --> 00:23:36.226
One, you're talking nonsense, two, you're
in no position to give anybody orders.

00:23:36.227 --> 00:23:37.427
Relax.

00:23:37.582 --> 00:23:40.148
We never should have let you come
out in the first place, all right?

00:23:40.227 --> 00:23:41.228
I'm trying to protect you.

00:23:41.306 --> 00:23:42.401
You protect me?

00:23:42.547 --> 00:23:44.751
I was hunting these woods when your
mommy was still kissing you good night.

00:23:44.752 --> 00:23:45.552
Yeah.

00:23:45.645 --> 00:23:48.398
It's a
damn-Near-Perfect hunter.

00:23:48.899 --> 00:23:50.620
It's smarter than you.

00:23:51.094 --> 00:23:56.492
And it's gonna hunt you down and eat you alive
unless we get your stupid sorry ass out of here.

00:23:56.523 --> 00:23:58.479
You know you're crazy, right? Yeah?

00:23:58.651 --> 00:24:01.268
You ever hunt -Chill out.

00:24:01.331 --> 00:24:05.508
Stop! Stop it. Everybody just stop.

00:24:06.295 --> 00:24:07.140
Look.

00:24:07.390 --> 00:24:09.847
Tommy might still be alive.

00:24:10.347 --> 00:24:12.913
And I'm not leaving here without him.

00:24:17.379 --> 00:24:19.491
It's getting late.

00:24:20.602 --> 00:24:23.027
This thing is a good hunter in the day,

00:24:23.637 --> 00:24:26.000
But an unbelievable hunter at night.

00:24:26.474 --> 00:24:28.758
We'll never beat it
--Not in the dark.

00:24:30.807 --> 00:24:33.154
We need to settle
inand protect ourselves.

00:24:34.140 --> 00:24:35.908
How?

00:24:45.407 --> 00:24:48.630
One more time.That's...?
Anasazi symbols.

00:24:48.786 --> 00:24:52.525
It's for protection. The
windigo can't cross over them.

00:24:53.453 --> 00:24:55.940
Nobody likes a skeptic, Roy.

00:25:06.354 --> 00:25:09.483
You want to tell me what's going
on in that freaky head of yours?

00:25:11.215 --> 00:25:13.296
Dean... No, you're not fine.

00:25:13.984 --> 00:25:16.503
You're like a powder keg,
man. It's not like you.

00:25:17.176 --> 00:25:19.867
I'm supposed to be the
belligerent one, remember?

00:25:23.881 --> 00:25:25.618
Dad's not here.

00:25:28.012 --> 00:25:33.555
I mean, that much we know for sure, right? He
would have left us a message, a sign, right?

00:25:34.447 --> 00:25:36.262
Yeah, you're probably right.

00:25:37.565 --> 00:25:40.381
To tell you the truth, I don't
think dad's ever been to Lost Creek.

00:25:42.211 --> 00:25:45.497
Then let's get these people back
to town, and let's hit the road...

00:25:45.768 --> 00:25:49.507
Go find dad. I mean, why
are we still even here?

00:25:58.175 --> 00:25:59.676
This is why...

00:26:00.099 --> 00:26:01.961
This book.

00:26:02.399 --> 00:26:07.692
This is dad's single most valuable possession.
Everything he knows about every evil thing is in here.

00:26:07.786 --> 00:26:10.070
And he's passed it on to us.

00:26:10.873 --> 00:26:13.689
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:26:14.675 --> 00:26:17.538
You know, saving
people, hunting things...

00:26:17.804 --> 00:26:20.057
The family business.

00:26:22.617 --> 00:26:24.072
That makes no sense.

00:26:24.229 --> 00:26:31.410
Why-Why doesn't he just call us? Why doesn't
he tell us what he wants, tell us where he is?

00:26:32.694 --> 00:26:34.321
I don't know.

00:26:36.011 --> 00:26:37.560
But the way I see it,

00:26:38.921 --> 00:26:42.144
Dad's given us a job to
do, and I intend to do it.

00:26:42.504 --> 00:26:43.834
Dean...

00:26:44.569 --> 00:26:45.461
No.

00:26:46.603 --> 00:26:48.214
I gotta find dad.

00:26:49.028 --> 00:26:51.031
I gotta find Jessica's killer.

00:26:56.953 --> 00:27:02.210
It's the only thing I can think about. Okay.
All right. Sam, we'll find them. I promise.

00:27:03.540 --> 00:27:04.718
Listen to me.

00:27:04.890 --> 00:27:07.018
You've got to prepare yourself.

00:27:07.925 --> 00:27:10.116
I mean, this search could take a while.

00:27:10.872 --> 00:27:12.578
And all that anger,

00:27:12.781 --> 00:27:16.364
You can't keep it burning over
the long haul. It's gonna kill you.

00:27:17.370 --> 00:27:19.310
You got to have patience, man.

00:27:21.848 --> 00:27:23.459
How do you do it?

00:27:24.257 --> 00:27:26.494
How does dad do it?

00:27:27.887 --> 00:27:30.202
Well, for one, them.

00:27:30.911 --> 00:27:35.135
I mean, I figure our family's so screwed
to hell, maybe we can help some others.

00:27:35.437 --> 00:27:37.721
It makes things a
little bit more bearable.

00:27:42.831 --> 00:27:44.881
And I'll tell you what else helps...

00:27:47.212 --> 00:27:51.155
Killing as many evil sons
of bitches as I possibly can.

00:27:53.796 --> 00:27:55.392
Help me!

00:27:58.583 --> 00:27:59.897
Please...!

00:28:04.208 --> 00:28:05.538
Help!

00:28:06.883 --> 00:28:08.401
It's trying to draw us out.

00:28:08.679 --> 00:28:10.135
Just stay cool. Stay put.

00:28:10.267 --> 00:28:12.306
Inside the magic circle?

00:28:12.395 --> 00:28:14.131
Help!

00:28:15.622 --> 00:28:17.187
Help me!

00:28:19.612 --> 00:28:21.614
Okay, that's no grizzly.

00:28:27.082 --> 00:28:30.179
It's okay. We'll be
all right. I promise.

00:28:33.688 --> 00:28:35.613
It's here.

00:28:42.142 --> 00:28:43.315
I hit it!

00:28:43.362 --> 00:28:44.395
Roy, no!

00:28:44.926 --> 00:28:46.053
Roy!

00:28:46.663 --> 00:28:48.024
Don't move.

00:28:52.284 --> 00:28:55.162
It's over here. Ugh!

00:28:56.795 --> 00:28:57.827
Roy?!

00:29:24.572 --> 00:29:25.621
I don't...

00:29:26.090 --> 00:29:29.078
I mean, these types of things--
They aren't supposed to be real.

00:29:29.313 --> 00:29:31.018
I wish I could tell you different.

00:29:32.228 --> 00:29:34.277
How do we know it's not
out there watching us?

00:29:34.809 --> 00:29:35.967
We don't.

00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:38.569
But we're safe for now.

00:29:39.993 --> 00:29:41.839
How do you know about this stuff?

00:29:44.405 --> 00:29:46.189
It kind of runs in the family.

00:29:51.871 --> 00:29:52.888
Hey.

00:29:53.983 --> 00:29:57.019
So, we've got half a
chance in the daylight.

00:29:57.320 --> 00:29:59.620
And I, for one...

00:30:00.105 --> 00:30:02.593
Want to kill this evil son of a bitch.

00:30:03.474 --> 00:30:05.351
Well, hell, you know I'm in.

00:30:05.763 --> 00:30:08.684
Windigo is a cree indian word.
It means, "evil that devours."

00:30:08.685 --> 00:30:10.285
They're hundreds of years old.

00:30:10.347 --> 00:30:16.625
Each one was once a man, sometimes an indian or
other times a frontiers manor a miner or hunter.

00:30:16.771 --> 00:30:19.931
How's a man turn into one of those
things? Well, it's always the same.

00:30:20.041 --> 00:30:21.449
During some harsh winter,

00:30:21.590 --> 00:30:24.985
A guy finds himself starving,
cut off from supplies or help

00:30:25.225 --> 00:30:29.793
Becomes a cannibal to survive, eating
other members of his tribe or camp.

00:30:29.871 --> 00:30:31.780
Like the donner party.

00:30:32.524 --> 00:30:36.298
Cultures all over the world believe that eating
human flesh gives a person certain abilities--

00:30:36.299 --> 00:30:39.299
Speed, strength, immortality.

00:30:39.383 --> 00:30:40.897
If you eat enough of it,

00:30:41.100 --> 00:30:43.385
Over years, you become this ...

00:30:43.588 --> 00:30:45.966
Less-Than-Human
thing.

00:30:46.129 --> 00:30:48.006
You're always hungry.

00:30:48.100 --> 00:30:51.949
So, if that's true, how
can Tommy still be alive?

00:30:54.124 --> 00:30:56.241
You're not gonna like it. Tell me.

00:30:56.569 --> 00:30:59.964
More than anything, a windigo knows
how to last long winters without food.

00:31:00.047 --> 00:31:03.082
It hibernates for years
at a time. When it's awake,

00:31:03.489 --> 00:31:06.654
It keeps its victims
alive. It stores them

00:31:06.983 --> 00:31:09.329
So it can feed whenever it wants.

00:31:10.456 --> 00:31:15.655
If your brother's alive, it's keeping
him somewhere dark, hidden, and safe

00:31:16.312 --> 00:31:18.158
And we got to track it back there.

00:31:18.299 --> 00:31:20.213
And then how do we stop it?

00:31:20.322 --> 00:31:21.402
Well,

00:31:21.668 --> 00:31:24.734
Guns are useless-So are knives.

00:31:25.756 --> 00:31:27.414
Basically...

00:31:27.821 --> 00:31:30.700
We gotta torch the sucker.

00:31:46.964 --> 00:31:47.981
Dean.

00:31:51.173 --> 00:31:52.299
What is it?

00:32:10.348 --> 00:32:11.615
You know,

00:32:11.960 --> 00:32:16.153
I was thinking that those claw
prints, so clear and distinct

00:32:17.800 --> 00:32:20.178
They were almost too easy to follow.

00:32:46.262 --> 00:32:50.000
You okay? His neck's broken.

00:32:50.736 --> 00:32:53.526
Run, run! Go, go, go, go, go!

00:33:02.696 --> 00:33:05.856
Come on. I got you. I got you.

00:33:15.740 --> 00:33:17.102
Hailey!

00:33:27.114 --> 00:33:28.428
Dean!

00:33:29.935 --> 00:33:33.517
If it keeps its victims
alive, why would it kill Roy?

00:33:33.721 --> 00:33:34.753
Honestly?

00:33:35.129 --> 00:33:38.274
I think because Roy shot
at it, he pissed it off.

00:33:45.883 --> 00:33:47.448
They went this way.

00:33:53.352 --> 00:33:55.495
It's better than bread crumbs.

00:35:37.674 --> 00:35:41.648
Hey, it's okay. It's okay. It's okay.

00:35:54.001 --> 00:35:55.159
Dean.

00:35:57.474 --> 00:35:58.945
You. Wake up.

00:35:59.810 --> 00:36:02.297
Dean. Hey. You okay?

00:36:04.863 --> 00:36:05.958
Yeah.

00:36:06.245 --> 00:36:08.529
Hailey... Hailey.

00:36:08.826 --> 00:36:10.923
Wake up. Wake up.

00:36:12.127 --> 00:36:13.270
Gotcha.

00:36:23.442 --> 00:36:26.431
You sure you're all right?
Yeah, yeah. Where is it?

00:36:26.530 --> 00:36:28.376
It's gone for now.

00:36:49.081 --> 00:36:49.957
Tommy.

00:36:53.477 --> 00:36:54.260
Tommy.

00:37:00.434 --> 00:37:02.030
Cut him down.

00:37:15.591 --> 00:37:17.375
We're gonna get you home.

00:37:18.287 --> 00:37:19.695
Check it out.

00:37:20.513 --> 00:37:23.048
Flare guns. Those will work.

00:37:37.500 --> 00:37:41.678
Looks like someone's home for
supper. We'll never out run it.

00:37:45.730 --> 00:37:48.202
You thinking what I'm
thinking? Yeah, I think so.

00:37:51.633 --> 00:37:54.251
All right, listen to me. Stay with
Sam. He's gonna get you out of here.

00:37:54.252 --> 00:37:55.952
What are you gonna do?

00:37:58.569 --> 00:38:01.244
It's chow time, you freakin' bastard!

00:38:01.573 --> 00:38:05.828
Yeah, that's right! Bring
it on, baby! I taste good!

00:38:13.799 --> 00:38:16.005
All right, come on. Hurry!

00:38:21.272 --> 00:38:22.508
Hey!

00:38:23.729 --> 00:38:25.997
Hey, you want some white meat, bitch?!

00:38:26.185 --> 00:38:27.515
I'm right here!

00:38:43.066 --> 00:38:44.680
Get him out of here. Sam, no.

00:38:44.681 --> 00:38:46.681
Go. Go!

00:38:47.071 --> 00:38:47.712
Go.

00:38:57.128 --> 00:38:58.067
Come on.

00:38:59.458 --> 00:39:00.413
Come on.

00:39:15.571 --> 00:39:16.447
Sam!

00:39:18.439 --> 00:39:21.552
Come on. Hurry, hurry, hurry! Go!

00:39:34.334 --> 00:39:35.836
Get behind me.

00:40:18.915 --> 00:40:21.199
Not bad, huh?

00:40:29.355 --> 00:40:34.643
That's when it circled the campsite. I mean,
this grizzly must have weighed 800, 900 pounds.

00:40:36.494 --> 00:40:39.779
So, really, I don't
know how to thank you.

00:40:42.960 --> 00:40:46.559
Must you cheapen the moment? Yeah!

00:40:47.588 --> 00:40:50.655
You riding with your brother? Yeah.

00:40:52.235 --> 00:40:53.299
Let's go.

00:41:05.375 --> 00:41:07.628
I hope you find your father.

00:41:10.971 --> 00:41:12.457
Thanks, Sam.

00:41:30.159 --> 00:41:32.458
Man, I hate camping.

00:41:32.771 --> 00:41:34.007
Me too.

00:41:37.172 --> 00:41:39.394
Sam, you know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:41:40.317 --> 00:41:42.382
Yeah, I know.

00:41:43.795 --> 00:41:46.017
But in the meantime

00:41:47.769 --> 00:41:49.537
I'm driving.



00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
